{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And they shall ask.</b> Elsewhere it says וישאלו (Exodus 12:35) [masculine], and here the females are mentioned, because it is the custom of women to ask of their neighbors more than the men [do] — utensils of gold and silver ornament, to place on the necks of sons and daughters, and nose-rings in ears and nose, bracelets and arm-ornaments and anklets. And this custom exists today in the land of Ishmael, not so in the land of the uncircumcised. And thus he mentioned a sorceress, for women practice sorcery more than men." "<b>And she empties her house.</b> For it was an inheritance to them [the Egyptians]. And there are some who complain and say that our ancestors were thieves — but those [who say so] do not fear [Heaven], for it was a command from on high. And there is no reason to ask 'why,' for HaShem created everything, and He gives wealth to whomever He wills and takes it from his hand and gives it to another, and this is not evil, for everything is His." "<b>And you shall despoil.</b> Like ודברתם (Numbers 20:8), for it is possible for its pattern to be from the nif'al binyan, like ונגפתם (Leviticus 26:17)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:31:29.200589856Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}